    "result": "Schema discovery: the three datasets map as `g1` = Office Products (13,933), `g2` = Electronics (top categories Computers, All Electronics, Camera & Photo, Cell Phones), `g3` = Musical Instruments (17,162). Review data lives in the `fdbk_*` tables (electronics = `fdbk_g2`); `prc` is stored in cents (verified: `prc/100 = prc_usd` for all rows having both).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"answer\": 8,\n  \"sql\": \"SELECT COUNT(*) AS answer FROM items_g2 i JOIN (SELECT ref_id, COUNT(*) AS review_ct, AVG(rtg) AS avg_review_rtg FROM fdbk_g2 GROUP BY ref_id) r ON r.ref_id = i.ref_id WHERE COALESCE(i.prc_usd, i.prc/100.0) > 50 AND r.review_ct >= 5 AND r.avg_review_rtg < 3.0;\"\n}\n```\n\n8 electronics products are priced above $50, have at least 5 reviews, and an average review rating below 3.0.",
